Hard rules — never invent:
- evidence_text MUST be a verbatim substring of the source text (copy the speaker's words).
  If you cannot quote support, omit the candidate.
- assertion_status (required):
    explicit — said directly ("I want to study in Germany")
    inferred — implied by evidence, not stated ("that university is too expensive" → cost sensitivity)
    uncertain — hedging ("I think", "maybe", "not sure")
    negated — rejection ("I don't want the US")
    hypothetical — conditional ("If I get a scholarship, maybe the US")
- attributed_to: "student" unless someone else is speaking or being quoted
  (parent, brother, counselor, friend). Never store another person's belief as the student's.
- Do not upgrade considering → decided, cheaper → chosen, or "brother thinks" → student thinks.
- Peer/social pressure (others doing X, outside influence on the goal): memory.observed,
  fact_type CONSTRAINT. attributed_to is who is influencing. Do not store someone else's wish as application.goals.
- Set is_correction=true when the text clearly updates a known fact (e.g. marks 847→877, budget 15k→25k).
- Set requires_confirmation for sensitive fields (passport, DOB, sponsor, finance details).
- Map to a catalog field_key when one fits. If nothing fits, use field_key memory.observed
  and fact_type OTHER_POTENTIAL_FACT — do not drop the fact.
- explicitness: explicit | strongly_implied | uncertain (keep in sync with assertion_status).
- Return empty fact_candidates only when the source has no potentially persistent information.

Living goal (current_goal) — classify meaning, not keywords. Any language
(English, Urdu, Roman Urdu, mixed). Do not translate the student's words.

kind:
- life_aim: they state a durable first-person life direction (study, work, move,
  program, destination). Shape, not a closed list:
  "I want to study locally in FAST" / "mujhe Germany jana hai" /
  "main FAST mein parhna chahta hoon" / "internship karna hai Dubai mein".
- turn_action: this-chat logistics or a request to you — attach/send/upload,
  find/look up, wait, lock a shortlist, "yeh attach karunga", "yeh dhoond do",
  "baad mein bhejta hoon", "I'll send it".
- none: greeting, question, acknowledgement, or no new direction.

A message can mix both. Then kind=life_aim and evidence_text is ONLY the aim
clause, never the attach/find/send clause.
stated=true only when kind is life_aim; otherwise stated=false and intent=null.
intent: the aim in THEIR words (keep Roman Urdu). evidence_text: verbatim
substring of the source. mode: pursuing | exploring.
supersedes_previous=true when they pivot (changed my mind / ab local nahi).
Hypotheticals, other people's aims, and negated aims → kind=none.

